+        <li><strong>Analytics (optional, off by default):</strong> only if you choose “Allow analytics” do we record the label of links and buttons you click and the time, sent to our analytics service on Google Cloud (USA). It doesn't include your name, account details or form contents, is never used for advertising, and never runs on sign-in or sign-up pages. If your browser sends a <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org/">Global Privacy Control</a> signal, analytics stays off and we don't ask.</li>
+        <li><strong>Your privacy choice:</strong> stored only in your browser's local storage so we don't ask again.</li>
+        <li><strong>Fonts:</strong> served from our own servers, so no third-party font provider receives your IP address.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Our pages tell your browser to send other sites only our domain name, never the page you were reading, and turn off browser features we don't use, such as camera, microphone, location and interest-based ad topics.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Your choices and rights</h2>
+    <p>You can change your analytics choice at any time: <button type="button" data-open-privacy-preferences class="underline cursor-pointer">Manage Privacy Preferences</button>. You can ask to access, correct or delete your account data at any time using the address in our <a href={`${baseUrl}legal/imprint`}>Imprint</a>. Deleting your account removes your username and password. Clearing your browser's site data removes your reading list cookie and saved privacy choice.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
